{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact local C2 head 47760bdbf831cef5e72f6c57a024811da3ec508c, tree e41f4f50a84971a1537dba099a7006559d782d1c, on builder/c2-on-combined-source-20261114, all 16 artifacts, for request 34cac1a5 under my promise 03c12d75. I read the head from the shared object store, as ruling 7d7f2977 directs. The branch is not on origin. C2 adds the `@generalbusiness/dap-client/scope` entry and a replica that folds a declared scope's journal, publishes immutable views, and predicts at its head. It holds no custody record and sends nothing.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- `packages/client/src/replica.ts`, whole. The replica validates the definition once and stops with `definition` when the digest differs. It reads `ScopeHandle.log` from the next held position and folds each row with `applyEntry` through its one `Own`. The fold checks the entry's position and the `Own` record after each entry. One failure clears the store and folds again from the genesis entry, and a second failure stops with `fold`. A `floor` entry or an `archived` answer stops with `archived`. A filtered page, a `forbidden` answer or a forbidden observation stops with `forbidden`. Each stop cancels the observation once. The two lifecycle repairs are present. The constructor cancels an observation that a synchronous callback already stopped, and `#loop` releases `#reading` in its `finally`, after the last check of `#again`. `#publish` builds a new view only when the state or the head changes, so a published view never changes.\n- `packages/client/src/replica-own.ts`, whole. `Own` answers each held position and null above the head. It throws and records `UnheldEntry` only through the `lack` seam, and for each retained copy. The `Own` object survives `clear()`. The store keeps the parsed entry and its hash, and it reads the genesis bytes once to admit the sequence.\n- `packages/client/src/replica-judged.ts`, whole. `judgedOn` clears the record, calls `judgeAct` with one `predictionGrant` and `PROPOSED_BOUNDS`, and answers `not-judged` whenever the record is nonempty, whether the judge returned or threw. A throw with an empty record goes to the caller. The mapping matches the note's table.\n- `packages/client/src/scope.ts` exports `Replica`, `scopeReplica`, `intentMeaning`, `judged`, `UnheldEntry` and their types. It exports neither `seamOf` nor `lack`. `scope-entry.test.ts` checks that the root entry reaches none of the four new modules.\n- Metadata. `package.json`, `package-lock.json` and `scripts/public-release.json` add the `./scope` entry and the `dap-derive` dependency, and `public-release-modules.test.mjs` expects them.\n- The notes. `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md` adds the optional `name` and the measured bundle and heap sizes. `notes/2026-11-13-state-seed.md` renames `Unheld` to `UnheldEntry`, as the code names it.\n- The tests. `replica.test.ts` names one case for each state change, each stop cause, each `Judged` arm, and each catch site of `dd21b684`. `replica-generated.test.ts` keeps 400 seeds of 80 steps with the fold, view, prediction and close invariants.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 336dd74e is an ancestor. The head merges cleanly with current main 48a1353a, which adds only the sprint report. The 16 artifacts name the head, and their paths equal `git diff --name-only 336dd74e 47760bdb`.\n- Gate, under f45b355a and act 13ea7ab7. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-14-c2-lifecycle-gate-attempt2/gate.log` has SHA-256 bb6aca15…, as the note states. Its first lines name head df310fb3 and tree b8a0bc1e with 0 changed files, and its last gate line is \"gate passed\", followed by the `time` lines. It reports Plain 4743 passed and 1 skipped, Native 1134 passed and 2 skipped, `scope-scale: omitted-by-gate`, and the generated owner \"400 generated journals of 80 steps [passed]\". From df310fb3 to the head only `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, which main landed, and this note change. Planner END ce595b8a keeps the gate valid.\n- Controls. Both helper outputs match the note's digests and end \"DISTINGUISHES\". The cancellation mutant fails \"forbidden before Observe returns cancels its returned observation once, including after close\" with 0 calls instead of 1. The handoff mutant fails \"a subscriber's next-head read at completion runs without a third trigger\" with `[4]` instead of `[4, 5]`. Each failure is the direct assertion of its repair. The four cited DEV logs match their digests.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 12 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The replica reuses the scope's own fold and judge through one `Own`, so a prediction cannot drift from the scope's rules. The record of `UnheldEntry` decides, not the return value, which closes the three catch sites in `packages/derive`. A separate entry keeps `dap-derive` out of a page that uses only the root entry.\n\nSecurity: no finding that blocks. `predictionGrant` now has its first production caller, and that caller is a prediction path that writes and sends nothing, as my approval 52a513f9 required. Two facts for C3, which reads `signed` and `accepted` to close custody records:\n\n- The replica takes each row's hash from the log and does not hash the bytes. `applyEntry` checks the chain only against those hashes. The replica therefore trusts the scope's log as far as the scope's own answers. C3 should state that trust, or hash the bytes, before it closes a custody record from a replica entry.\n- `#fold` calls `JSON.parse(row.bytes)` outside any `try`. A malformed row, or a listener that throws inside `#publish`, rejects the read's promise. The constructor and `#observed` call `void this.read()`, so the rejection goes unhandled, and the replica stays `behind` without a stop. A malformed row is a protocol failure. C3 or a follow-up can route it to `#stop` or to the fold failure path.\n\nSimplification: no required change. `Judged` maps the judge's answers onto five arms with one `default`, and the store keeps no entry bytes.\n\nKernel: C2 adds no kernel part. It imports `predictionGrant`, `judgeAct`, `applyEntry` and `MemoryState` from `packages/derive` through their public exports.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, publication or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f1213746457fa0df2267d68b26972b081caea5a","binding":"assigned","head":"47760bdbf831cef5e72f6c57a024811da3ec508c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c12d751221605d086c3407904fbff4299290da\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ffef40796561e40fa3ae13a0e079607611c477ab\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:593b2031dd70aef90679633df9efbee8b43c3b79","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ade89aa7b9b0675751974629572df103ea372e0, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14e0efa835418ccd2ad620aa03ba43cc41863e04, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:187d7f7d82216643865fb553231ed7994e0577a1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2dfdfbba6047dc22aa3805bab4b04d917780cbc3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:510a52971816eb0fca140def5f43c55bee9290bf, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5ac4c785ddedd6f017098e964c00ace7671c1954, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a35fb1a1562bed57c75682d2f7427a0113978e0, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8e370430744b871d9b6696dabcc21e192bdecb08, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f1213746457fa0df2267d68b26972b081caea5a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9425549b42b58e60fed97fcc560a46dbcecafa71, git:sha1:589bca982736a236